From 4878154a1e95df75263f2a15e0b6e44e5b49d078 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:54:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Fix Kanban wait-notice board counts and unused-grant
 ready clocks

Wait notices and card reads counted host workers without their board: the other-board sum excluded the process's
current board (default) instead of the connection being read, so a runners notice said 0/7 busy while default ran
7. They also opened other boards through writable/migrating connections and turned a read failure into a partial
sum. And a Board grant claimed and returned unused reset the ready clock to the release time (ready@1794369068 for
a card waiting since 1794351914).

- kanban_host_counts: board of the connection, other boards opened mode=ro, any failure => running unknown.
- queue position / notices carry board, observed_at and an admission reason or explicit unknown.
- _last_ready_entry_ts, ready_since and the chat-wait SQL prefilter ignore unused-grant runs and their claimed
  events; actual execution, loss and ready transitions still reset it.

Priority advice was already relative-only (kanban_priority.advice); no fixed --priority 10 remains.
Incidents: default/t_01a1c6809ba7fc32, runners/t_01a1c7d517a4477a, default/t_01a1c6c56a99c3e1. Card t_01a1ce30a39b7172.
